---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CropProtectionNav from "../../components/CropProtectionNav.astro";
import ProductLookup from "../../components/ProductLookup.astro";
import SeasonalMonitor from "../../components/SeasonalMonitor.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Crop Protection Reference | Aman Poonia" description="A traceable crop-protection reference prototype for Punjab.">
  <CropProtectionNav />
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Punjab crop-protection reference</p>
    <h1>Identify first. Decide with evidence.</h1>
    <p class="lede">A static reference prototype for crops, pests, pesticide formulations, product compositions, and documented decision support. The first vertical slice is Kinnow and citrus psylla around Abohar.</p>
    <p><a href="/crop-protection/crops/kinnow/">Browse Kinnow</a> · <a href="/crop-protection/pests/citrus-psylla/">Identify citrus psylla</a> · <a href="/crop-protection/assistant/">Assess a situation</a></p>
  </section>

  <SeasonalMonitor />

  <section>
    <h2>Start With What You Know</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card"><p class="eyebrow">1. Identify</p><h3><a href="/crop-protection/pests/citrus-psylla/">I found insects, eggs, or damage</a></h3><p>Compare life stages, visible features, likely months, look-alikes, and beneficial organisms before considering treatment.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><p class="eyebrow">2. Browse</p><h3>Choose a crop</h3><p>Use the <strong>Browse crop</strong> menu above to view seasonal monitoring priorities, plant parts to inspect, and evidence-backed options. Kinnow is the first available crop.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><p class="eyebrow">3. Assess</p><h3><a href="/crop-protection/assistant/">I know the pest</a></h3><p>Record pest pressure and earlier products. The prototype explains what is known, unknown, excluded, or not preferred.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What Does My Product Contain?</h2>
    <p>Search a known catalog product by brand, manufacturer, ingredient, composition, or formulation. You must select a displayed entry; a typed name is never treated as product data.</p>
    <ProductLookup />
  </section>

  <section class="note">
    <strong>Evidence boundary:</strong> seasonality identifies what deserves inspection. It does not prove that a pest is in your orchard, that an action threshold is crossed, or that a pesticide should be applied. Current labels remain controlling for any application.
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
